# Swift / iOS project-rule (template)

Replace `{{APP_NAME}}`, bundle IDs, and module names. **Keep only one tier** (Small, Medium, or Big) when creating the active rule.

---

## How to choose a tier

| Tier | When to use |
|------|-------------|
| **Small** | MVP, internal app, 1–3 devs, fast iteration |
| **Medium** | Production consumer/B2B app, ongoing product team |
| **Big** | Enterprise, compliance, many modules/teams, long lifecycle |

---

## Tier: Small project

### S1. Scope

- Prefer **clarity** over heavy architecture. **SwiftUI** + **`@Observable` / `ObservableObject`** or simple **MVVM** is enough.
- One **target**, one **module** unless Apple mandates extensions (widgets, etc.).
- **SwiftLint** optional; **SwiftFormat** optional — if used, run in CI or pre-commit.

### S2. Layout

```
{{APP_NAME}}/
├── App/
│   └── {{APP_NAME}}App.swift
├── Views/
├── ViewModels/          # optional; views may hold light state
├── Services/            # API, keychain, analytics
├── Models/
└── Resources/
```

### S3. Concurrency and networking

- Prefer **`async/await`** and **`URLSession`** (or Alamofire if already in project).
- **MainActor** for UI updates; avoid blocking the main thread.
- Use **`Codable`**; handle **decoding errors** with user-visible fallbacks.

### S4. State and navigation

- **`NavigationStack`** with simple routing enum or string tags acceptable.
- **UserDefaults** for trivial prefs; **Keychain** for tokens (use a small wrapper).

### S5. Testing and quality

- **Xcode build** must succeed with **no warnings** policy only if team agrees; otherwise fix critical warnings.
- **Unit tests** for parsing, pricing, auth helpers — where mistakes hurt users.
- No secrets in source; **XCConfig** + CI for API keys.

### S6. Checklist (small)

- [ ] No force-unwraps in production paths without documented reason.
- [ ] Sensitive data in Keychain; not logged.
- [ ] Basic error UI for network failures.

---

## Tier: Medium project

### M1. Scope and architecture

- **MVVM** or **MVVM-C** as default: Views → ViewModels → Services/Repositories.
- **Dependencies point inward**: UI does not call URLSession directly from every view — use **protocol-oriented** services (`AuthServiceProtocol`, etc.).
- **Feature folders** encouraged:

```
Features/
├── Home/
│   ├── HomeView.swift
│   ├── HomeViewModel.swift
│   └── HomeCoordinator.swift   # if using coordinators
├── Profile/
└── ...
Core/
├── Networking/
├── Persistence/
├── DesignSystem/
└── Utilities/
```

### M2. Swift style

- **`private` / `fileprivate`** by default; widen access deliberately.
- Prefer **`struct`** for models and value types; **`class`** for identity or Objective-C interop.
- **Line length** ~120 or team standard; use **SwiftFormat** config in repo.
- **Explicit `self`** only when required; avoid **implicitly unwrapped** optionals in new code.

### M3. Networking and data

- **Typed endpoints** (enum or struct per resource); central **APIClient** with interceptors (auth refresh, logging).
- **DTOs** separate from **domain models** when API shape ≠ app concepts; map in repository layer.
- **Pagination** and **cancellation** (`Task` cancel) for lists.

### M4. Navigation

- **Coordinator** or **Router** pattern for deep links and auth flows if complexity grows.
- **Single place** for **session** state (logged in / out) driving root `View` swap.

### M5. Error handling

- **Typed errors** (`enum AppError: LocalizedError`) or **Result** in service layer.
- Map to **alert** / **toast** / **inline** consistently with design system.

### M6. Dependency injection

- **Constructor injection** for ViewModels and services; avoid **singletons** except for `APIClient` / `Analytics` if documented.
- Consider **Factory** or lightweight container if object graphs grow.

### M7. UI

- **Design tokens**: colors, typography, spacing in one module.
- **Accessibility**: Dynamic Type, VoiceOver labels on interactive controls, contrast.
- **Images**: async load + placeholder; **Kingfisher** or **Nuke** if remote images are heavy.

### M8. Testing

- **Unit tests**: ViewModels (with mocked services), parsers, reducers.
- **UI tests**: critical journeys (login, checkout) on CI simulator.
- **Snapshot tests** optional for design-system components.

### M9. Security

- **Certificate pinning** when product requires; document bypass for debug only.
- **App Transport Security** exceptions documented and minimal.

### M10. Schemes, crash reporting, and feature flags (medium baseline)

Production-oriented medium apps treat these as **standard**.

- **Environments (`dev` / `staging` / `prod`)**: **Xcode schemes** + **xcconfig** per configuration; **separate** bundle identifiers / app groups where the product needs side-by-side installs or different API hosts. **API base URLs**, analytics keys, and flag SDK keys read from **build settings** or **generated** `Info.plist` entries — not a single hard-coded prod URL in source.
- **Crash and performance**: **Firebase Crashlytics**, **Sentry**, or equivalent in **Release**; **dSYM** upload / **symbolication** automated in CI. Add **performance** instrumentation (Firebase Performance, MetricKit summaries, or custom OS_signpost traces) for **launch** and **critical** user journeys; watch **staging** metrics before promoting.
- **Feature flags**: **Firebase Remote Config**, **LaunchDarkly**, **Unleash**, or internal API — **document** flag keys, defaults per environment, owners, and **cleanup** after full rollout.

### M11. Checklist (medium)

- [ ] Feature folders; no cyclic imports.
- [ ] Services behind protocols; mockable in tests.
- [ ] Localization for user-facing strings (`Localizable.xcstrings` / strings files).
- [ ] CI runs build + unit tests.
- [ ] **Schemes/config**: behavior verified on the correct **dev / staging / prod** configuration.
- [ ] **Crash/performance**: release symbols wired; no PII in breadcrumbs/logs.
- [ ] **Feature flags**: new flags documented with removal plan when temporary.

